TodoApp: Cross-Platform Task Management System


Project Overview
TodoApp is a high-performance mobile application designed to facilitate efficient task management and real-time productivity tracking. Built using the React Native framework, the application leverages a modern tech stack to ensure a responsive user experience and secure data persistence.

Core Functionality
User Authentication: Implements secure user onboarding and session management via Firebase Authentication.

Persistent Storage: Utilizes a cloud-based NoSQL database for real-time data synchronization across multiple sessions.

Date-Centric Task Management: Integration of a dedicated calendar interface for scheduled task tracking and deadline visualization.

Responsive Interface: Employs a utility-first styling approach to ensure UI consistency across various Android screen densities.

State Management: Efficient handling of application state to ensure low-latency interactions during CRUD operations.

Technical Specifications
Development Environment: Visual Studio Code (VS Code)

Framework: React Native (CLI Workflow)

Backend-as-a-Service: Firebase (Firestore and Auth)

External Libraries: React Native Calendar (NPM) for date management

Build Tool: Gradle (Android)

Development Workflow
The project was developed using the React Native CLI to maintain full control over the native Android build configuration. Development was conducted within Visual Studio Code, utilizing the integrated terminal for dependency management and build execution. The architecture follows a modular component structure, integrating third-party NPM packages to extend functionality while maintaining optimal performance.

Deployment and Installation
The source code for this project is currently maintained in a private repository. However, the compiled application is available for testing and evaluation.

Navigate to the Releases section of this repository.

Download the latest version of the application package (app-release.apk).

Transfer the file to an Android device.

Enable installation from unknown sources in the device security settings.

Execute the file to complete the installation.

Developer Information
The application was developed by an Electronics and Communication Engineering student specializing in full-stack mobile development and cloud integration. This project demonstrates proficiency in JavaScript environments, mobile backend integration, and native build optimization.
